# Discipline policy — <PROJECT>

**What this is.** A single set of rules: which tool is enabled BEFORE which event, what counts as
"done", and a journal of deliberate relaxations. ⛔ Under the guard — edits go through the owner's key.

The gate (`scripts/gate.sh`) executes these rules with one command. Here — *why* and *when*.

---

## 1. Triggers "tool BEFORE the event"

A tool is wired in BEFORE what it catches appears in the code — not after an incident.

| What appears in the code… | …wire in BEFORE it | Catches |
|---|---|---|
| A new DB query / model / relation | N+1 detector (django-zeal) | lazy reloading in a loop |
| A new external HTTP call | timeout + retry + error handling | eternal waiting, a silent failure |
| A new module/layer | a contract in `.importlinter` | an import "to the wrong place", blurring of seams |
| A decision that is expensive to reverse | an entry in `docs/adr/` in the form `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/presets/adr.md.template` | "why is it so" asked again every half year |
| A new public function/class | a docstring (ruff D) | an undocumented API |
| A comment or docstring | what the code does now, in the present tense; the story of the change goes to the commit message and the journals (`prose_content`) | a comment retelling the session that wrote it |
| User input/form | validation + a test on hostile input | injections, crashes |
| A secret/token | reading from env/file (never into code/log) | a leak into git/output |
| Branching logic | a test on every branch (100% coverage) | an uncovered path |
| A mechanism that "fires" | a counter-case "and here it must not fire" | a rule that fires ALWAYS |
| A new seam between components | a scenario test THROUGH a real joint | a suite that is green over a broken system |
| A new test | a mutant run: break what is guarded, see red | a test that checks nothing |
| A test longer than the baseline timeout | a marker in `pyproject.toml` + a line in `conftest.py` (both under the guard — edit through the owner's key) | quietly growing run time |

*(Add rows for the specifics of <PROJECT>.)*

