## 2. Definition of Done

A task is closed only when EVERYTHING is done:

- [ ] There is an issue in the tracker, a branch `issue-<N>-<slug>`, commits reference `#<N>`.
- [ ] State labels are current (a STEP of the cycle, not memory): start → `in-progress` (`ready` removed); finish → `gate-passed`+`review-clean` → closing via `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/bin/retainer-task-close.sh <owner/repo> <N>` (removes the working label in the same call; `retainer-preflight` checks the closed ones for a tail).
- [ ] The plan, review findings, **grooming decisions and open questions** of the active task are IN THE ISSUE BODY (durable, AS WORK GOES; canon = the body, edit-in-place, not a stream of comments), not in an ephemeral scratchpad/only-in-chat/memory: on compaction/pickup the context must survive. When picking up — **re-verify the body** (the task order may have changed). Dependencies — by a native `#N` ref, expand **lazily** (pull a linked issue only when taking it into work, not the whole tangle).
- [ ] The plan was checked by `plan-checker` BEFORE code (verdict "plan ok" / contradictions removed).
- [ ] The prose of new files and of the lines a change adds is in Latin script if the project declared this with the `prose_lang` key
      (docstrings, comments, definition names; user-facing text — in the user's language).
      If you write prose in another language — the key is `false`, and this item does not apply. A CASE docstring is
      mandatory on a par with production code: the relaxation is dropped only for the module and package docstring.
- [ ] A comment or docstring the change adds describes behaviour: what the unit does, what a parameter means, what
      constraint holds. A task number, what the code used to do, what broke or was measured on the way go to the
      commit message, the research journal or the error journal. A date or a number stays only as the measured fact
      a threshold rests on. The gate's `prose_content` step names such lines in what a change adds, in every
      project, with no key to turn it off; `retainer:allow-prose` on the line lifts one false finding.
      The step cannot tell "a key used to sign requests" from history: write "a key that signs requests".
- [ ] `scripts/gate.sh` is green locally (all steps, without `--no-verify`) — ONE full run, on
      what leaves the machine. While editing, the subject is judged by a targeted run and a mutation
      probe (`bash ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/bin/retainer-mutate.sh`), not the full suite for every
      hypothesis.
- [ ] `code-reviewer` BEFORE the commit: remarks cleared or entered in the debt journal.
- [ ] CI is green on an environment from scratch (not only locally).
- [ ] Documents updated (`doc-updater`): epic status, architecture, this policy if the rules changed.
- [ ] PR → merge → issue closed on merge.

